{"pages":{"project-a":{"title":"Big Love","kicker":"PROP DESIGN / CASE STUDY","body":"A focused prop-design case study showing how research, fabrication, finish, and performer needs are translated into objects that feel specific to the production.","sections":[{"order":1,"image_side":"left","image_url":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1617013377476-e4596b777264?auto=format&fit=crop&w=2400&q=82","image_alt":"Cat sitting across a computer keyboard","header":"THE OBJECT HAS A JOB","subheader":"RESEARCH, STORY, FUNCTION","body":"Every prop begins by answering a dramatic question. References establish period and tone, while scale, construction, and handling are planned around the action the performer actually has to repeat."},{"order":2,"image_side":"right","image_url":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1781873492280-4ed33df82f48?auto=format&fit=crop&w=2400&q=82","image_alt":"Rubber ducks wearing sunglasses and bright red lips","header":"THE FINISH CHANGES IN LIGHT","subheader":"SURFACE, SHEEN, CONTRAST","body":"Paint and texture are judged under theatrical light, where a subtle surface may disappear and a glossy one may flare. Final adjustments keep the object believable inside the full stage picture."}]},"project-b":{"title":"The Servant of Two Masters","kicker":"PROP DESIGN / SELECTED WORK","body":"A concise visual record of selected prop work for the production, presented as a simple image study of materials, character, scale, and stage presence.","sections":[{"order":1,"image_side":"left","image_url":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1734549343493-c4f08ea3afee?auto=format&fit=crop&w=2400&q=82","image_alt":"Vintage-styled dog dressed like a person reading a letter","header":"","subheader":"","body":""},{"order":2,"image_side":"right","image_url":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1782560769841-df6ddda6570b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=2400&q=82","image_alt":"Cat paw resting dramatically on a computer mouse","header":"","subheader":"","body":""},{"order":3,"image_side":"